From 66cc4407d3d764e3e2d7b4bbd9c99cf703e1357c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:15:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Replace gnu-keyring.gpg with gnucobol-keyring.pgp, the keyserver copy of
the key that signs releases (B9459D0CA8A740B323235CDF13E96B53C005604E),
because sqv cannot use the old keyring: it holds 10 v3 (PGP 2) keys,
which Sequoia does not parse, so sqv rejects the whole file (GnuPG skips
such keys silently). The other certificates in it are dropped (541
certificates of other people). Its Source line names the new file
instead of https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gnu-keyring.gpg, which is not what
the file holds any more.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore           |   1 -
 gnucobol-keyring.pgp | 278 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gnucobol.spec        |   4 +-
 sources              |   1 -
 4 files changed, 281 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gnucobol-keyring.pgp

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index c749e98..a90d57c 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 /gnucobol.tar.gz
 /gnucobol-3.1-rc1.tar.gz
 /gnucobol-3.1-rc1.tar.gz.sig
-/gnu-keyring.gpg
 /newcob.val.Z
 /gnucobol-3.1.1.tar.gz
 /gnucobol-3.1.1.tar.gz.sig
diff --git a/gnucobol-keyring.pgp b/gnucobol-keyring.pgp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..28c43b0
--- /dev/null
